            <ArticleTitle>Acquired Brown's syndrome in systemic lupus erythematosus: another ocular manifestation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>399-400</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Tenosynovitis in rheumatic disorders may affect ocular muscles producing symptoms unfamiliar to rheumatologists. We present a case of superior oblique tenosynovitis (Brown's syndrome) as an early rheumatic manifestation in a patient with systemic lupus erythematosus.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
